Aight, lemme break it down real quick. Do a trial division from 2 up: while i*i <= n, keep divvin' out i as long as n % i == 0 and collect i each time. After that, if n > 1, that leftover is a prime — push it too. Join all collected primes with '*' and you good.

Tiny Python example you can run:

def factors(n):
    res = []
    i = 2
    while i * i <= n:
        while n % i == 0:
            res.append(str(i))
            n //= i
        i += 1
    if n > 1:
        res.append(str(n))
    return '*'.join(res)

